      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The approach that focuses on systemic injustices and power struggles is more effective for kids, as it prepares them for the complexities of the real world and encourages critical thinking about the ongoing struggles for equality and justice. By acknowledging the darker aspects of history, students can develop empathy and a deeper understanding of the ongoing impact of these injustices, rather than blindly celebrating national triumphs. This approach also helps to foster a more nuanced and informed citizenry, rather than one that is swayed by simplistic patriotism.",
